<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  THE PER-STRIP NARROW TOGGLE (proposal 48 M2, AC2.2 / AC2.3 / D9).

  NARROW KEEPS M/S/R, THE METER AND THE FADER, and hides the name text beyond
  an elision, the inserts and the sends. It is not a density ladder: the head's
  Full/Compact/Tiny exists because a lane's HEIGHT is imposed on it by the
  arrangement, whereas a strip's width is the user's own two-state choice.

  THIS DEVIATES FROM D9 ABOUT WHERE THE FLAG LIVES, and the deviation is what
  makes this case possible at all. D9 says the flag "cannot" live on the track
  — "narrow is a per-USER view preference and STrack attributes are serialized
  with the arrangement" — and prescribes a pane-owned set joined to
  `SStdMixerView::pruneUiState`. Both halves are stale:

    - `pruneUiState()` was RETIRED by proposal 46 M3; only tombstones remain,
      so there is no walk to join;
    - the three sets D9 names as still being in it (`takesExpanded_`,
      `trackScale_`, the shown-automation set) all moved onto STrack in that
      same milestone, and every one is a per-user view preference serialized
      with the arrangement. The reason D9 gives excludes those four equally.

  D9's own next sentence is the one that survives: "if the narrow flag can live
  on the track, it needs no pruning at all." It can, so it does — a fifth
  sibling of the four, serialized only when true.

  TWO THINGS THAT FOLLOW, and both are asserted below rather than assumed:

    1. THE FLAG NOW SURVIVES A FRESH PANE. Every seam builds one (shell
       inv. 62), so under D9's pane-owned set a toggle would have been
       invisible to the very next assertion — which is exactly why M1's
       mixer_inserts had to say it could not assert narrow at all.
    2. AC2.3's HAZARD CANNOT ARISE. A dangling key inherited by a later track
       allocated at the same address is impossible when there is no key: the
       flag dies with the object. Asserted anyway, because "cannot arise" is
       a claim about the implementation and this checks the behaviour.

  This case touches no `mixer/*` INI key and so owns none.
-->
<SActionScript version="1" name="mixer_narrow_strip">
  <actions>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="0" name="Alpha"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="1" name="Beta"/>
    <add-send-lane sendName="Reverb"/>

    <!-- ============ AC2.2: WHAT NARROW KEEPS AND WHAT IT DROPS ======== -->

    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="narrow=0"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="inserts=1"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="sends=1"/>

    <mixer-strip-toggle track="Alpha" control="narrow" on="true"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="narrow=1"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="inserts=0"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="sends=0"/>
    <!-- ...and the meter is still there, which is the half that makes narrow
         a useful width rather than a hidden strip. -->
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Alpha" contains="lanes=2"/>

    <!-- ============ IT IS PER STRIP, NOT PANE-WIDE ==================== -->

    <assert-mixer-pane track="Beta" contains="narrow=0"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Beta" contains="inserts=1"/>

    <!-- ============ AND IT LAYS OUT CLEANLY MIXED ==================== -->
    <!-- One narrow strip beside two wide ones, on both axes. -->

    <assert-mixer-layout paneWidth="640" paneHeight="260" stripWidth="96"
                         maxCrushed="0" maxOverlap="0"/>

    <!-- ============ AC2.3: THE FLAG DIES WITH ITS TRACK =============== -->
    <!-- Alpha is narrow. Remove it and add a new track: the newcomer is WIDE.
         Under a pane-owned STrack*-keyed set this is the exact case that
         inherits a dangling key when the allocator reuses the address. -->

    <remove-track trackPath="0"/>
    <drain-pending-deletes/>
    <add-track index="-1"/>
    <set-track-name trackPath="1" name="Gamma"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Gamma" contains="narrow=0"/>
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Gamma" contains="inserts=1"/>

    <!-- ...and Beta, which was never narrowed, is still wide. -->
    <assert-mixer-pane track="Beta" contains="narrow=0"/>
  </actions>
</SActionScript>
